# rfc-008-reporting-dashboard.mdc

## Title
RFC 008 – Reporting & Analytics Dashboard

## Summary
This RFC outlines the structure and components of an analytics dashboard designed for Admin and Team Lead roles. It provides insight into platform usage, video/course performance, and user activity.

---

## Goals
- Track video/course engagement metrics
- Show completion stats per user and per course
- Identify inactive or low-engagement users/content

## Metrics to Display
### For Admin
- 📊 Top 10 Most Viewed Videos
- 📈 Course Completion Rate (overall and per course)
- 🧍‍♂️ Most Active Users (based on watch logs)
- 🚨 Incomplete Mandatory Courses (with approaching deadlines)

### For Team Lead
- 📊 Completion stats for own team
- 📉 Least completed courses by team
- 🕒 Average time to complete a course

## Database Views / Aggregations
### SQL Views (suggested)
- `view_video_stats` → video_id, total_views, avg_watch_time
- `view_course_stats` → course_id, completion_rate, avg_duration
- `view_user_engagement` → user_id, total_watch_time, last_activity
- `view_incomplete_mandatory` → user_id, course_id, deadline, days_remaining

## UI Components
- Admin/Lead Dashboard route: `/admin/analytics` or `/team/analytics`
- Cards with stats summary (e.g. charts, numbers)
- Tables for detailed listings
- Filters by team, date, course, etc.

## Permissions
| Role        | Permissions                            |
|-------------|-----------------------------------------|
| Admin       | View all analytics                     |
| Team Lead   | View only analytics of own team        |
| User        | ❌ No access                            |

## Timeline
**Sprint 8**
- Define SQL views and test queries
- Build dashboard UI with chart and table components
- Integrate with `watch_logs`, `courses`, `assignments`
- Implement filters and role-based access

